Evelyn,<br />
<br />
The Novarra export is attached as a matter-record report with the document =
list. What we hold on 2011-0284: the April 4, 2011 engagement letter; the a=
rbitration demand, statements, expert reports and the panel's interim rulin=
g; and the February 2014 settlement agreement and closing letter. Fourteen =
profiled documents in all, plus billing data in the accounting system.<br /=
>
<br />
What is not there: correspondence. The matter's email trail runs March 2011=
 through February 2014, which is entirely before the January 1, 2014 corres=
pondence cutoff of the 2016 Casebridge migration - CommsStore content was o=
ut of scope and did not come over. There is no scope amendment, no suppleme=
ntal engagement letter, and no note of any limitation among the profiled do=
cuments. The Matter Scope field reads, in full: "Representation of Torvane =
Industrial Group, Inc. in connection with claims arising out of the Kelling=
 Station Unit 2 expansion project." That text was populated at migration fr=
om the engagement letter itself, per NOV-2119; the old Casebridge free-text=
 Scope Note field, whatever it said, was not carried.<br />
<br />
So on what the DMS holds, the engagement reads as unlimited and stayed that=
 way. I want to be clear that this is a statement about what survived the 2=
016 migration, not about what happened - for pre-2014 email the retention c=
opy is the mail journal archive, not Novarra. Howell can speak to that side=
.<br />
<br />
Anika
